MC This code uses filter to select ________ and select to select ________
```
print(dat
	|> filter(conductivity > 500)
	|> select(transect_no, position, plant_species, conductivity)
)

```

observations; observations

* observations; variables

variables; observations

variables; variables

MC How would you change the code below to include all observations where conductivity _might be_ > 500?
```
print(dat
	|> filter(conductivity > 500)
)
```

|> filter-out(conductivity < 500)

|> filter-out(conductivity != 500)

* |> filter-out(conductivity <= 500)

|> filter-out(conductivity > 500)

MC What picture would the following ggplot code produce (you can test this with riparianData if you want)?
```
print (ggplot(dat)
	+ aes(x=wet, y=plant_species)
)
```

Nothing

Just a blank square

* Axes showing wet and plant_species, but no data plotted

A plot of the relationship between plant_species (on the y-axis) and wet (on the x-)

SA What do you think would happen if we add color to our position histogram from the virtual lecture (see below). You are encouraged but not required to test it out.
```
print (ggplot(dat)
	+ aes(position, color=plant_species)
	+ geom_histogram()
)
```
